  reasoning:['Why is avoiding unnecessary neck movement important at this point?',
   ['Movement across an unstable injury can worsen cord or nerve damage','The injury’s stability is unknown, and neurologic symptoms are already present. Protect alignment during assessment and essential transfers.'],
   ['Motion restriction guarantees that no fracture occurred','It reduces avoidable motion while the injury is evaluated. It cannot identify whether there is a fracture.'],
   ['Pain relief permanently prevents secondary neurologic injury','Analgesia is important for comfort. It does not stabilize a potentially injured spine.'],
   ['Neck movement matters only after complete paralysis develops','Incomplete deficits may progress. Preventing unnecessary movement is valuable before severe loss occurs.']],
